<description>&lt;p&gt;Violence persists across South Sudan, with armed groups ambushing civilians in Jebel Boma County and killing two people, and a road ambush in Warrap County killing five. In Juba, a central bank employee was killed, a plane crash left three survivors, and the airport manager was removed in an internal reshuffle. Women in Greater Mundri appealed for protection after attacks, while a Christian woman was killed after refusing a forced marriage to a Muslim man, and two pastors were injured in a separate attack. The Jonglei governor reported ongoing efforts to end clashes in Bor, Duk and Twic East, and elections were postponed again to February 2027. According to UCDP, there were two battle-related deaths in 2024.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxNUzVVZlh0cUIxWFBYU2NGYnZWdHZmc1RLY3oyNm51NTlQQjJEMFlVclNsN2tWM0FjMmRycVdsMXQ2WW4xeUJZYVR1V3lac2ZBTmJ4RWcxYXVxaFlGV1dNbXM3OG5FOXhheVdiM0dzUVktZnJZZkQxNUU4ZWZuM0lWV2JyZXVKUXZtcDl2RHVaTVRtRGN1ZFdPckdPQ0dZSFI1SDVfVGlPbWhYa0o0alNCNFdsSDgtUkhxakRWZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Reuters&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxPT2FRa1pCeDZMbTZNUV9TRl9wdFl2OFRWZGhXQXZyYkVxYVNnYkl6US02bHNrUG9NYXRtZHFURUJvMld2aVA1LXlBQmNKd2pFeWx6NDZ2LUROY0w1RDVfQUZsOWo3bW9WaFdtSXl5WlFXQ2Zlc3lWWERGNW1wSGRhSkp2RGxPWDNJUTdKcHBVeGlCcDZ0X1Vn?oc=5&quot;&gt;FTL Somalia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinwFBVV95cUxPMlVPbjFTU3JSamhueTdqVmMtVXlxS0lrYlI3N09kVEVHRno5RmNnTW9qVVgyc2ZpTDg3RGk5Yjk1b01OV2tLejhTUzlKcG9INlR0aWdWd0loSEk4LW5MdGllLVhoV3BseU9kc09RcGR1VVpORUZMYm1aNVByb0JxVFBidWtWcHNfZDRWT2h3N0xqZ3laYmtLQTdJMlB6UWc?oc=5&quot;&gt;Morningstar News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Social News XYZ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a